we are seeing the same issue when using differential loading with v8 and this is breaking in es5 script bundles in IE 11 for specific instances where we have multiple class inheritances without constructor defined in some of the classes.

ex:
`
export class A {
constructor(public dep1: SomeType){}
}

export class B extends A {
}

export class C extends B {
constructor(dep1: SomeType, dep2: AnotherType){
super(dep1);
}

ngOnInit(){
//this.dep1 is undefined here
//this.dep2 is defined
}
}
`

bumping, the exact same problem, but specifically only in IE11.

We have a component that extends an abstract class that injects `ComponentFactoryResolver` (to resolve dynamic components), and it worked before in IE11; now the dependency is `undefined` in the component.

```
abstract class WrapperComponent {
  constructor(
    private componentFactoryResolver: ComponentFactoryResolver
  ) {
  }
}

class AComponent extends WrapperComponent {
  
}
```

By the way, if you use `Injector` directly, DI works as it should (with `@angular/core` v8.2.14).

```ts
import { Injector, Injectable } from '@angular/core';

class Dependency {
  prop1 = 'this is dependency property';
}

@Injectable()
class Parent {
  constructor(public dependency: Dependency) {}
}

@Injectable()
class Child extends Parent { }

const injector = Injector.create({providers: [
  {provide: Dependency, deps: []},
  {provide: Parent, deps: [Dependency]},
  {provide: Child, deps: [Dependency]}
  ]});

console.log(injector.get(Child));
```

See [stackblitz](https://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-angular-issues-31337?file=index.ts)

